    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can I reverse a WhatsApp divorce?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'If the talaq sent by WhatsApp has been registered at court, the husband can revoke it (raj\'i) during the iddah period, approximately three months, without needing a new nikah contract, provided it was a revocable (first) talaq. The revocation should be documented and communicated to the wife. If the iddah has lapsed, the couple would need a new nikah contract to remarry. If the talaq was a third (final) divorce in a third separate marriage, UAE law does not permit remarriage without the wife having an intervening marriage.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Does WhatsApp divorce affect my visa in UAE?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'A registered divorce, regardless of how it was initiated, affects your visa if your UAE residence was sponsored by your husband. You have a grace period after the divorce certificate is issued (typically 30-60 days per GDRFA rules) to arrange alternative sponsorship. An unregistered WhatsApp divorce has no visa consequences because legally, the marriage has not ended. Do not leave the UAE or cancel your visa based on an unregistered WhatsApp message alone.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What about email or voice note divorce?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Email and voice note divorces follow the same legal logic as WhatsApp: they can constitute a valid talaq pronouncement if intent is clear, under Federal Law No. 5/1985 and Federal Law No. 1/2006. Voice notes have been accepted in UAE courts, though authentication is more complex, voice analysis may be ordered. Email divorces are admissible under e-transactions law. All require court registration within 15 days under Article 58 of Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Is an Instagram DM divorce valid in UAE?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'In principle, yes, an Instagram direct message containing a clear divorce declaration can be a valid talaq pronouncement under the same framework that governs WhatsApp and SMS. UAE courts apply the communication-of-intent test regardless of the platform. Authentication of Instagram DMs is more complex than WhatsApp screenshots, but Meta\'s law enforcement portal provides authenticated message data to courts with valid orders. All the same registration requirements apply.',
      },
    },
  ],
